      },
      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "single-file",
      "text": {
        "source": "",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "Transcoded from examples/WebServer.orch (C17) into Rust by scripts/transcode_webserver.py to test the Rust generator. Same topology, routes, limits and access log; only the bodies, the libraries and the type field types differ. The C17 specification follows.\n\nWebServer \u2014 a single-process HTTP/1.1 server expressed as a Wirecraft C17 dataflow network.\n\nPURPOSE\nServe three fixed routes plus a fallback, demonstrating typed links, a self-feedback loop,\nlibrary instances lent by dependency links, and composite routing.\n\nCONFIGURATION (environment, read once at start)\n- WEBSERVER_PORT: TCP port, default 8080 (1\u201365535).\n- WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY=1: listen on every IPv4 address; otherwise loopback 127.0.0.1 only.\n- WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS=N: request shutdown after N resolved requests; 0 or unset = unlimited.\nSIGINT/SIGTERM also request shutdown through the generated runner.\n\nROUTES\n| Method   | Path          | Status | Content-Type                  | Entity              |\n| GET/HEAD | /home/about   | 200    | text/plain; charset=utf-8     | routeHomeAbout      |\n| GET/HEAD | /home/version | 200    | text/plain; charset=utf-8     | routeHomeVersion    |\n| GET/HEAD | /api/user     | 200    | application/json              | routeApiUserDetails |\n| other    | known path    | 405 (+ Allow: GET, HEAD)                | routeNotFound       |\n| any      | unknown path  | 404                                     | routeNotFound       |\n| \u2014        | unparsable request line | 400                           | routeNotFound       |\nThe query string is ignored for matching. HEAD returns the GET header without a body.\nEvery response carries Content-Type, Content-Length, Connection: close and Server.\n\nFLOW (one ReqRep packet per request)\nsocket_accept --request--> router --route*Request--> route --route*Response--> socket_respond\n--response--> socket_accept, which writes the reply and closes the connection.\nWhile a request is in flight its pending copy circulates on awaitResponseLoop.\n\nOWNERSHIP OF ReqRep STRINGS (packets are copied by value)\n- The pending copy on awaitResponseLoop owns id, request.header and request.body.\n- Router and route copies only borrow those strings.\n- The route allocates response.body; socket_respond allocates response.header.\n- socket_accept frees both sets exactly once when it resolves the request\n  (lib_http_server.http_resolve). content_type always points to a string literal.\n\nLIMITS AND ERRORS\nHeader \u2264 8 KiB (else 431), body \u2264 64 KiB by Content-Length (else 413), 2 s receive timeout\n(408 when nothing arrives, 400 on a truncated request). These connections are answered by the library and never enter the network.\nAllocation or socket failures end the run with THREADWORK_ERROR; the process exits non-zero.\n\nEXECUTION MODEL AND LIMITATIONS\nSingle-threaded cooperative loop: each tick runs every entity once and each link moves at most\none packet. When nothing is pending, socket_accept waits up to 25 ms for a connection, so an\nidle server does not spin. Reading a request blocks for up to 2 s per connection, so a slow\nclient delays others. No TLS, keep-alive, chunked encoding or IPv6.\n\nSHUTDOWN\nAfter shutdown is requested, socket_accept stops accepting, resolves every pending request,\nthen closes the listener; the runner's drain ends once no packet moves.\n\nACCESS LOG\nsocket_accept prints one line per resolved request on stdout:\n\"<id> <method> <path> <status> <body bytes>\"; startup prints the listening URL.\n",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "Build: compile with wirecraft.compile_c17 into a new directory, then\n  clang -std=c17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic WebServer.c -o webserver\nRun: WEBSERVER_PORT=18080 WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS=6 ./webserver\nExpect (curl -s -i):\n1. GET /home/about   \u2192 200, text/plain, body names the example.\n2. GET /home/version \u2192 200, text/plain, body \"WebServer 0.1.0 (Wirecraft C17)\".\n3. GET /api/user?x=1 \u2192 200, application/json, valid JSON with \"name\":\"Ada Lovelace\".\n4. GET /missing      \u2192 404, body \"404 Not Found: /missing\".\n5. POST /home/about  \u2192 405 with \"Allow: GET, HEAD\".\n6. HEAD /home/about  \u2192 200 header with Content-Length of the GET body and no body.\nAfter the sixth request the process exits 0 and has printed six access-log lines.\n",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
