    {
      "id": "node_b3fdad12-aa8a-4d1f-a50c-bc43654bb903",
      "name": "socket_accept",
      "kind": "Processor",
      "parentId": "root",
      "children": [],
      "incomingLinks": [
        "992f1269-5aa2-4929-91a3-5745c23f6cb9",
        "link_47dfe6fa-791b-4863-99ff-002db0ff8f88",
        "link_559f3fef-7b5a-4d0e-9d55-8f70aa5c46b8",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "outgoingLinks": [
        "link_66e6e8e4-5fb1-4171-8bc9-1d22a4323ec5",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "x": 222.32325019058075,
        "y": 1098.441268190992,
        "width": 200.0,
        "height": 138.0,
        "closedWidth": 200.0,
        "closedHeight": 138.0,
        "openWidth": 200.0,
        "openHeight": 138.0,
        "isExpanded": true
      },
      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
      "text": {
        "source": "// Counters that a C body keeps in statics live in the run context.\nlet mut sequence = *context.state::<u64>(\"socket_accept.sequence\");\nlet mut resolved_total = *context.state::<u64>(\"socket_accept.resolved\");\nlet limit = *context\n    .state::<Option<u64>>(\"socket_accept.limit\")\n    .get_or_insert_with(|| {\n        std::env::var(\"WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS\")\n            .ok()\n            .and_then(|text| text.parse().ok())\n            .unwrap_or(0)\n    });\n// Both buffers of the awaitResponseLoop self-link hold the pending copies.\nlet pending = [awaitResponseLoop_in, awaitResponseLoop_out];\n\n// 1. Resolve every response against its pending copy, rotating each loop buffer once.\nwhile !response.is_empty() {\n    let item = pop::<ReqRep>(response)\n        .ok_or(\"webserver: response buffer holds a value that is not a ReqRep\")?;\n    let mut found = false;\n    for side in pending {\n        for _ in 0..side.len() {\n            let waiting = pop::<ReqRep>(side)\n                .ok_or(\"webserver: pending buffer holds a value that is not a ReqRep\")?;\n            if found || waiting.id != item.id {\n                push(side, waiting);\n                continue;\n            }\n            found = true;\n            if libhttp.http_resolve(&waiting, &item) != 0 {\n                eprintln!(\"webserver: client closed the connection early\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    if !found {\n        return Err(format!(\"webserver: response {} has no pending request\", item.id).into());\n    }\n    resolved_total += 1;\n    if limit > 0 && resolved_total >= limit {\n        threadwork_runner.shutdown_request();\n    }\n}\n// 2. Accept at most one connection; wait briefly only when nothing is in flight.\nlet idle = awaitResponseLoop_in.is_empty() && awaitResponseLoop_out.is_empty();\nif threadwork_runner.is_running() {\n    if libhttp.http_wait(if idle { 25 } else { 0 }) {\n        sequence += 1;\n        if let Some(accepted) = libhttp.http_accept(sequence) {\n            push(request, accepted.clone());\n            push(awaitResponseLoop_out, accepted);\n        }\n    }\n} else if idle {\n    libhttp.http_close();\n}\n*context.state::<u64>(\"socket_accept.sequence\") = sequence;\n*context.state::<u64>(\"socket_accept.resolved\") = resolved_total;",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "let port: i64 = match std::env::var(\"WEBSERVER_PORT\") {\n    Ok(text) if !text.is_empty() => text.parse().unwrap_or(0),\n    _ => 8080,\n};\nlet any_address = std::env::var(\"WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY\").as_deref() == Ok(\"1\");\nif let Err(error) = libhttp.http_listen(port, any_address) {\n    eprintln!(\"webserver: cannot listen on port {port}\");\n    return Err(error.into());\n}\nlet host = if any_address { \"0.0.0.0\" } else { \"127.0.0.1\" };\nprintln!(\"webserver: listening on http://{host}:{port}\");",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "Entry and exit point of every request.\n\nInitialization: read WEBSERVER_PORT and WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY, open the listener with\nlibhttp.http_listen and print \"webserver: listening on http://<address>:<port>\".\nFailure to listen is an error (the process exits non-zero).\n\nEach tick:\n1. Pop every resolved ReqRep from `response` and find its pending copy by id in the\n   awaitResponseLoop self-link. Both of its buffers (awaitResponseLoop_in and\n   awaitResponseLoop_out) are searched by rotating each once, so the copies that do not\n   match keep their order. Resolve the match with libhttp.http_resolve (write the reply,\n   log it, close, free). A response without a pending copy is an error.\n2. While running, accept at most one connection with libhttp.http_accept and push the new\n   ReqRep to both `request` (router) and awaitResponseLoop_out (pending copy). Wait up to\n   25 ms for a connection only when nothing is pending.\n3. Count resolutions; at WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS request shutdown.\nAfter shutdown, stop accepting and close the listener once nothing is pending.",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "- With an unused port, startup prints the listening URL and the process keeps running.\n- With the port already in use, initialization fails and the process exits non-zero.\n- Two concurrent clients receive the responses matching their own requests (ids differ).\n- WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS=1 exits 0 after exactly one access-log line.",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
